<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:18:48 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Indonesia: Second ferry disaster in five days</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days</link><description>
At least one person has died and more than 100 people remain missing after a ferry carrying 243 people sank in rough weather between the Indonesian islands of Java and Borneo. The disaster is the second major ferry accident in the region in five days, renewing concerns over safety standards, overcrowding and maintenance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2167cbc-af62-11f1-84e0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-121016-121213-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e2167cbc-af62-11f1-84e0-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-121016-121213-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e6e73e0c-af62-11f1-a370-6ba72121faf5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:17:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen: Fighting escalates around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait</link><description>
Fighting is escalating in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi forces seized strategic territory around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, prompting counterstrikes by government forces and reported Saudi air raids. The Houthis also claimed attacks inside southern Saudi Arabia and threatened to disrupt shipping through the key maritime chokepoint, raising fears for regional security and global trade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abc04a1a-af6e-11f1-819a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-140115-140311-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abc04a1a-af6e-11f1-819a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-140115-140311-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b0d9495c-af6e-11f1-acd2-8d251d540f38</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:15:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government</link><description>
As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d325c64-af53-11f1-8d54-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20799631186aa669301c83e0-07656090.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5d325c64-af53-11f1-8d54-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-20799631186aa669301c83e0-07656090.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efc97ae-af71-11f1-a226-7db7cf189a1f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:11:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Radio France staff strike over appointment of far-right weekly editor</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-radio-france-staff-strike-over-appointment-of-far-right-weekly-editor</link><description>
Staff at public broadcaster Radio France began a two-day strike on Sunday over the appointment of Charles Sapin, deputy editor-in-chief at far-right weekly Valeurs Actuelles. Unions accuse Sapin of promoting far-right ideas ahead of next spring's presidential election, while management has defended the appointment in the name of pluralism.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02d53bbe-af04-11f1-9d7b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e1d9fdbe2d48d1241c3b6d21d639c8533611857e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02d53bbe-af04-11f1-9d7b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e1d9fdbe2d48d1241c3b6d21d639c8533611857e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ef9108e-af70-11f1-8f8f-7db7cf189a1f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:44:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02d53bbe-af04-11f1-9d7b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/e1d9fdbe2d48d1241c3b6d21d639c8533611857e.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race</link><description>
Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ece2006-af62-11f1-9504-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-120821-121000-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7ece2006-af62-11f1-9504-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-120821-121000-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83e41de8-af62-11f1-a945-0121a29fa1cc</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:08:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive</link><description>
A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images, from commemorations marking 25 years since the 9/11 attacks to the breakthrough win for Germany's far-right AfD party and the lightening offensive that has left Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels in control of the country's Red Sea coast.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ae8a078-adc2-11f1-b7b9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7YH9LY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ae8a078-adc2-11f1-b7b9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7YH9LY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a126d980-adec-11f1-88fe-45e2e454489d</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:48:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ae8a078-adc2-11f1-b7b9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7YH9LY.jpg">© Leonardo Munoz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sweden election: A turning point for the far right?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right</link><description>
The stakes are high in Sweden's general election, with the far right poised to enter government for the first time. TV4 News journalist Markus Karlsson-Bourrioux explains how opinion polls shifted from a comfortable centre-left lead to a tight race over the summer, and how far-right ideas have gained ground since the last election in 2022.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426517d8-af57-11f1-b8a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-110343-110655-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/426517d8-af57-11f1-b8a8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-110343-110655-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">470ce630-af57-11f1-9a1a-e5cb8c8e2679</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:48:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Germany: Thousands rally against far-right after AfD victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory</link><description>
Tens of thousands of people marched in around 20 cities across Germany to protest the rise of the far right after the AfD's historic victory in the Saxony-Anhalt state election. Demonstrators said they were defending democracy as mainstream parties continue to rule out governing with the AfD.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94b4a34-af4d-11f1-9e44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-100840-101014-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94b4a34-af4d-11f1-9e44-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-100840-101014-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be44bef8-af4d-11f1-a7d9-892c781611bd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:41:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>BRICS summit: What came out of the New Delhi meeting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting</link><description>
The BRICS summit in New Delhi ended with a joint declaration calling for greater Global South influence in global governance and urging restraint in the Middle East. The gathering also served as a platform for one-to-one diplomacy, with leaders holding a series of bilateral meetings aimed at easing regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bc26e46-af52-11f1-bd45-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-080107-080556-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1bc26e46-af52-11f1-bd45-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-080107-080556-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21143122-af52-11f1-b2e8-892c781611bd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:27:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>UK: Police probe £72 million donation to Reform UK</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-uk-police-probe-%C2%A372-million-donation-to-reform-uk</link><description>
British police have opened a criminal investigation into a £72 million donation to Nigel Farage's Reform UK, amid questions over whether the funds breached rules on foreign political donations. The probe comes as anti-immigration protests and counter-demonstrations intensify across England, highlighting growing tensions over immigration and national identity.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7248a62-97a8-11f1-96cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215404300241.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7248a62-97a8-11f1-96cf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215404300241.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c55cae8-af4e-11f1-8466-73f69d7693eb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:26:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Macron, Carney to visit North Atlantic French islands after Trump's map post</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney will reaffirm the “sovereignty of nations” on a visit on September 20 to Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory in the North Atlantic, the Élysée Palace announced on Sunday. The symbolic trip comes after US President Donald Trump posted a map on social media showing the entire North American continent covered by the US flag.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07123c12-af55-11f1-9ad5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/df646ee48064e65458879e443f4be68f8b225f7d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07123c12-af55-11f1-9ad5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/df646ee48064e65458879e443f4be68f8b225f7d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08b45cd0-af55-11f1-a91e-e5cb8c8e2679</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:25:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07123c12-af55-11f1-9ad5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/df646ee48064e65458879e443f4be68f8b225f7d.jpg">© Evelyn Hockstein, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen: Houthi offensive triggers new displacement crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis</link><description>
More than 70,000 people have fled their homes in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi rebels launched an offensive to seize the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, with many escaping to Aden and around 1,400 crossing into neighbouring Djibouti. The UN and IOM warn the new displacement wave is worsening an already dire humanitarian crisis in a country devastated by 12 years of war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4a391aa-af4c-11f1-89fe-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-100133-100308-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4a391aa-af4c-11f1-89fe-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260913-100133-100308-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa040cba-af4c-11f1-8c92-892c781611bd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:18:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France apologises for diplomatic spat with US to lift block on new ambassador to Washington</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-france-apologises-for-diplomatic-spat-with-us-to-lift-block-on-new-ambassador-to-washington</link><description>
The French UN mission said it regretted an online post criticising a US vote at the UN General Assembly in a move that should clear the way for the new French ambassador Aurélien Lechevallier to take up his post in Washington.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8728c102-af4e-11f1-9048-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2P7793.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8728c102-af4e-11f1-9048-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2P7793.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c8e07e2-af4d-11f1-8c62-892c781611bd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:01:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8728c102-af4e-11f1-9048-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2P7793.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>On Sept 12th, 'everyone was compassionate': The world needs 'to be together again' - Richard Roeill</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Richard Roeill, former New York Firefighter and 9/11 First Responder. His testimony reframes the legacy of September 11th not as a historical event confined to a single day, but as living history. The former New York City firefighter describes an anniversary that reactivates trauma, while the illnesses suffered by first responders make the consequences of Ground Zero ever present decades later. Yet Roeill’s testimony is not simply a narrative of sacrifice. He says that responders were misled about the dangers they faced, demanding accountability and long-term healthcare for those exposed to the very toxic air.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b09ae3ac-af40-11f1-8f49-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4831165916aa649db9d44f8-98355403.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b09ae3ac-af40-11f1-8f49-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4831165916aa649db9d44f8-98355403.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e37993c-af43-11f1-9f8f-4f396abe40f0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 07:18:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Olympic rematch: US and France to meet for women's FIBA World Cup title</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-olympic-rematch-us-and-france-to-meet-for-women-s-fiba-world-cup-title</link><description>
France won against host Germany in the women's FIBA World Cup semifinals Saturday and will now face the United States in the final Sunday after the four-time defending champion and tournament favorite defeated Spain in the other semifinal.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/233acfba-aec6-11f1-9581-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84P8ZF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/233acfba-aec6-11f1-9581-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84P8ZF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e911bcae-af3d-11f1-a592-0529a93c31a8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:48:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/233acfba-aec6-11f1-9581-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C84P8ZF.jpg">© Tobias Schwarz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Swedes vote in close general election that could usher far right into government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government</link><description>
Swedes are heading to the polls Sunday for a general election that will either bring a far right party into government for the first time or shift the country back towards the liberalism it has long been known for. The centre-left opposition holds a narrow lead over the ruling right-wing bloc but Prime ⁠Minister Ulf Kristersson's four-party alliance – which includes the far right Sweden Democrats – has been catching up in the final weeks of campaigning.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">033aa45a-af3a-11f1-a91a-0529a93c31a8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 06:16:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84572cd0-af39-11f1-afd7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7XT2GD.jpg">© Jonathan Nackstrand, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East live: Houthis say hit Saudi base after renewed fighting with Yemeni forces</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260913-middle-east-live-houthis-say-hit-saudi-base-after-renewed-fighting-with-yemeni-forces</link><description>
Yemeni Houthi rebels claimed responsibility on Sunday for an attack on a military base in southern Saudi Arabia as renewed fighting with Yemen's government forces forced growing numbers of civilians to flee. Fighting in western Yemen over the past few weeks has left hundreds dead and displaced tens of thousands of people. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e97ed2ba-adc3-11f1-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253315512845.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e97ed2ba-adc3-11f1-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253315512845.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8d278f7e-af31-11f1-8a91-8764f0e8196c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:11:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e97ed2ba-adc3-11f1-b34d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253315512845.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>'Second life': Nepal hydropower tunnel survivor recalls ordeal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal</link><description>
Nepali hydropower worker Sanjay Sah survived in total darkness inside a tunnel flooded by the deadly flash flood that struck the China-Nepal border on August 26, drinking muddy water and praying that rescuers would find him. The survivor, who was rescued on September 4, recalls the 10 days he spent stranded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd66cb94-af4b-11f1-b7c9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/6e02499a819e924052703d50c7a7f3df5ac351ba.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd66cb94-af4b-11f1-b7c9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/6e02499a819e924052703d50c7a7f3df5ac351ba.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">004d6efe-af2a-11f1-bc02-2d0ec09addbf</guid><pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 04:17:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd66cb94-af4b-11f1-b7c9-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/6e02499a819e924052703d50c7a7f3df5ac351ba.jpg">© Deepesh Deo Joshi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia closes East-West pipeline as Houthis tighten grip on Red Sea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260912-saudi-arabia-shut-down-east-west-pipeline-as-houthis-tighten-grip-on-red-sea</link><description>
Saudi Arabia on Saturday ​shut down the vital East-West pipeline after the conduit came under attack in the widening Middle East war, threatening to send energy prices soaring. The 1,200-km pipeline has served as the main route out for global ​supplies of Middle East oil for the ‌past six months while the Strait of Hormuz has been largely shut by war.
